From edf1d0a6f44ae2b6afb89b826565e9d2c73e66c9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 18:25:01 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 31/94] ASoC: codecs: add the HiBy hm100 FPGA DAC

The HiBy RS6 DAC is a Gowin GW1N-9 FPGA (hm100) behind an NJW1195A
volume controller. The driver loads the FPGA bitstream over JTAG/SPI
from firmware (the stock kernel's own data and checksum, picked by
IDCODE), sets the sample rate, output routing and power sequencing as
the stock 1.80 kernel does, follows the jack switches, and exposes gain,
digital filter, NOS and volume controls.

